proton_raw:
Solar Activity: 
Low solar activity is expected to continue with a chance of isolated Moderate-class flares.



Solar Wind / Geomagnetic Activity: &nbsp;
In the absence of any geoeffective coronal holes or Earth directed CMEs solar wind speeds are expected to remain at background. Geomagnetic activity will be Quiet to Unsettled with a chance of Active intervals on Day 1 (4 Aug).&nbsp;


Energetic Particles / Solar Radiation:&nbsp;GOES18 &gt;10MeV proton flux is expected to continue at Background with no further enhancement currently forecast..

Solar Activity: 
Low solar activity is expected to continue with a slight chance of isolated Moderate-class flares.



Solar Wind / Geomagnetic Activity: 
In the absence of any geoeffective coronal holes or Earth directed Coronal Mass Ejections, solar wind speeds are expected to reduce to Background on Day 1 (05 Aug), though Enlil suggests they could increase to Slightly Elevated on Day 4 (08 Aug) due to a possible glancing blow from a Coronal Mass Ejections . Geomagnetic activity is likely to be Quiet to Unsettled (Kp0-3), although there is a small chance it could increase on Day 4 (08 Aug) due to a possible glancing blow from a Coronal Mass Ejection or connection to Coronal Hole. This is very low confidence.&nbsp;



Energetic Particles / Solar Radiation: 
GOES18 &gt;10MeV proton flux is expected to continue at Background.&nbsp;

Solar Activity:&nbsp;
Low or Very Low activity is expected to continue, with further Common class flares likely to continue until the region in the far northwest rotates across the western limb.



Solar Wind / Geomagnetic Activity:&nbsp; 
Slightly elevated solar winds probably declining back to Low levels. A further CME arrival is then possible with a glancing impact on day 2-3 (11-12 Aug). This is due to the 08 Aug north-centre disc filament eruption, although any observed arrival is low confidence, with the CME mainly passing north of Earth. However this could arrive alongside the onset of weak fast winds. Geomagnetic activity is expected to be mainly Quiet. However any CME glance or fast wind onset later on day 2 or day 3 (11-12 Apr) will bring a further chance for a spell of Unsettled to Active geomagnetic activity with a probability of isolated Minor Geomagnetic Storm intervals.



Energetic Particles / Solar Radiation: 
The count rate of energetic particles (high energy protons) is expected to persist at Background.

Solar Activity: 
Activity is expected to remain Low, with only a slight chance of an isolated M-class flare.&nbsp;



Solar Wind / Geomagnetic Activity:
 CH86/+ is expected to connect with Earth from later Day 1 (13 Aug), or more likely through Day 2 (14 Aug), but this is also low confidence.&nbsp;


Geomagnetic activity may increase late Day 1 (13 Aug) or more likely through Day 2 (14 Aug) upon connection to CH86/+, to bring a likelihood of Active intervals and a chance of G1/Minor geomagnetic storms, which may also continue into Day 3 (15 Aug), before gradually waning on Day 4 (16 Aug).&nbsp; &nbsp;



Energetic Particles / Solar Radiation: 
GOES18 &gt;10MeV proton flux is expected to continue at Background.
